uggestion","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"In the fields of computational linguistics and probability, an n-gram is a contiguous sequence of n items from a given sequence of text or speech. The items can be phonemes, syllables, letters, words or base pairs according to the application. The n-grams typically are collected from a text or speech corpus. When the items are words, n-grams may also be called shingles.[1]  An n-gram of size 1 is referred to as a \"unigram\"; size 2 is a \"bigram\" (or, less commonly, a \"digram\"); size 3 is a \"trigram\". Larger sizes are sometimes referred to by the value of n, e.g., \"four-gram\", \"five-gram\", and so on.","topics":[],"score":212154,"global_rank":273642},{"name":"xinghai-zhang/Mhacks6","owner":"xinghai-zhang","html_url":"https://github.com/xinghai-zhang/Mhacks6","stars":1,"forks":0,"watchers":1,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"Automatically generates powerpoint from news articles on the web.","topics":[],"score":212130,"global_rank":273709},{"name":"kridos/FounderScraper","owner":"kridos","html_url":"https://github.com/kridos/FounderScraper","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":212122,"global_rank":273733},{"name":"crteal/pauline","owner":"crteal","html_url":"https://github.com/crteal/pauline","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":"\"Good movies make you care, make you believe in possibilities again\"","topics":[],"score":212122,"global_rank":273736},{"name":"NOAA-PMEL/ecofoci-sst-highres-comp","owner":"NOAA-PMEL","html_url":"https://github.com/NOAA-PMEL/ecofoci-sst-highres-comp","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"language":"Python","description":null,"topics":[],"score":212122,"global_rank":273740},{"name":"Zhuoli/scrips4macapp","owner":"Zhuoli","html_url":"https://github.com/Zhuoli/scrips4macapp","stars":0,"forks":0,"watchers":0,"issues":0,"lan